  "revision": "2026-07-28.1",
  "note": [
    "CROSS-LANGUAGE PARITY FIXTURE. The declarative validation rules exist twice: in",
    "@lukeflow/form-core (TypeScript, runs in the browser) and in luke-core-engine's",
    "SubmissionValidator (Java, the server-side backstop that a tampered payload cannot skip).",
    "Two implementations is a deliberate trade — the alternative was running a JS runtime on the",
    "JVM — and THIS FILE is what keeps them honest: every case below runs in BOTH.",
    "",
    "  form-core : packages/form-core/src/validation/parity.test.ts  (validateValue)",
    "  core-engine: SubmissionValidatorParityTest                    (validateTyped)",
    "",
    "A case is { id, type, attributes, value?, valid, code? }. `type` is the entity type and is",
    "merged into the attribute bag exactly as the engine does. An ABSENT `value` key means",
    "undefined. `code` is the expected failure code and is asserted only when valid=false.",
    "",
    "CHANGING THE RULES: edit this file, bump `revision`, and update the matching constant in the",
    "Java test. The revision assert is what catches 'rules changed in one language only' at review",
    "— the two repos have no shared CI, so nothing else would.",
    "",
    "OUT OF SCOPE (client-only by design, NOT a parity gap): expressions, author JS, async/minion",
    "validation, and cross-field conditionals. The server never evaluates those."
  ],
